  data: {
    LLM: "Play proceeds clockwise from the dealer's left. On your turn, play one card that matches the rank or suit of the top card on the play pile, or draw one card from the stock if you cannot play. Breaking a rule incurs a penalty card. First to empty their hand and call 'Mao' (or 'game over') wins. Rules vary by group and are often learned by trial and error.",
    Player: "Play proceeds clockwise from the dealer's left. On your turn, play one card that matches the rank or suit of the top card on the play pile, or draw one card from the stock if you cannot play. Breaking a rule incurs a penalty card. First to empty their hand and call 'Mao' (or 'game over') wins. Rules vary by group and are often learned by trial and error.",
    objective: "Be the first to shed all cards. When you play your last card, you must yell 'Mao!'.",
    gameplay: "Play proceeds clockwise from the dealer's left. On your turn, play one card that matches the rank or suit of the top card on the play pile, or draw one card from the stock if you cannot play. Breaking a rule incurs a penalty card. First to empty their hand and call 'Mao' (or 'game over') wins. Rules vary by group and are often learned by trial and error.",
    keyRules: [
      'Match the top card on the play pile by rank or suit; or draw one from stock if unable.',
      'Call Mao or game over when playing your last card.',
      'One penalty card per rule breach; the person giving it states what was wrong without explaining the rule.',
      'Rules vary by group and are learned by observation and trial and error.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
